<title>UK: Ladbroke firm on talk of stake purchase.</title>
<headline>Ladbroke firm on talk of stake purchase.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Ladbroke Group Plc rose on Tuesday as a report in the Financial Times highlighted prospects for a sizeable purchase of the company's stock by Hilton Hotels Corp.</p>
<p>Ladbroke shares were up 2p at 234 by 0923 GMT in volume of 1.7 million shares.</p>
<p>The FT said Hilton was committed to buying a five percent stake in Ladbroke yet could not buy after the end of June, since the company will be in &quot;closed&quot; period ahead of its results, during which time directors are barred from buying shares in a company.</p>
<p>No-one at the hotels-to-gaming company was immediately available for comment on the FT report.</p>
<p>Hilton last week raised $375 million in an issue of ten-year bonds.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
